    },
    {
      "id": "1fc15869407b3b3314bda86fecf08f7614b4f50d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1735275362,
          "type": null,
          "body": "More precise terminology would be \" display filter expressions,\" (most of which are fields but not here) but the misnomer is used in the code already. The meaning of display filter expressions and possibly the validity of the current filter has changed.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-01-21T02:40:35.678Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-21T02:40:35.678Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 276502097,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14117,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "6ea5903b0a0df70eb53d6409733866d162ada221",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1735275635,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The signal is normally emitted when fields are registered (or deregistered) by a dissector's UAT, but it's the same signal that needs to be sent when a change in display macros affects the display filter language.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-01-21T02:44:28.000Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-21T02:44:28.000Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 276502097,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14117,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "be5fb56cb723538bafaf65ef4084c98e70a46a5d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1735276432,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> The signal is normally emitted when fields are registered (or deregistered) by a dissector's UAT\n\n\"By a dissector\" suffices; not all fields generated at dissector startup time (as opposed to fields statically defined in an `hf[]` array) come from a UAT.  The RADIUS dissector, for example, generates them from FreeRADIUS files it reads.\n\nBut what it really means is that \"something happened that causes the syntax of valid display filters to change\", which would include changes to the set of named fields as well as to macros or other user-defined syntactical items.\n\nAt some point, the name(s) should probably be changed to make it clearer that this can happen even if *no* dissector has changed its set of registered fields.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2024-01-21T02:54:24.122Z",
          "updated_at": "2024-01-21T02:54:24.122Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 276502097,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 14117,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5a420cea08a004396504240027488b3a827d0383",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1735277143,
          "type": null,
          "body": "(And I tend to refer to those expressions as \"packet-matching expressions\", as they're used in places that don't involve filtering packets out of the display, such as coloring rules.)",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
